A||||8||fropuff||Removing trim w/o busting clips?||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||07-06-2001||01:36 AM||||Hey.  I know I should have done this when I got my car painted, but I've decided to repaint my black molding.  I've already bought new $50 clips once, and I don't want to do it again.  I'm wondering if there's a way to remove the trim w/o breaking the clips.  I know the trim comes off the clips w/o problems, but I also want to take the clips out to put the molding back on.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Smoooooth GT||07-06-2001||02:10 AM||||Fropuff..  HHHmmm.. Why not just leave it off and I'll SMOOOTH  IT OUT for you...lol<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/big_wing_and_vette_light's.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG">   <BR>  with a 100-125HP shot of NOS...||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||07-06-2001||02:10 AM||||Nope........I have removed a LOT of trim pieces and once in a great while a clip comes off undamaged but more often than not they simply break......I'm sure Roger Garrison would agree on this one.....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||07-06-2001||11:21 AM||||I'm going to be repainting my car in the very near future. Can someone tell me off the top of my head how many clips there are? Or am I going to actually have to do some work?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <BR>TIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-06-2001||01:46 PM||||Yep, gonna break more than not. Newer cars are even getting worse. (ie) Honda side moldings, if you take them off, every clip is gonna break and there molded into the molding. new paint=2 fender moldings and all the door moldings 2 or 4 door. at a cost of about $75 each. There made to go on at the factory fast not ever to come back off. So they stay on now unless there already damaged.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cplensdorf||07-06-2001||03:10 PM||||My car is getting a final 'rub' as I type this.  I just removed all of the body side molding with only one broken clip (although I think it was broken before I started) The trick is to get a piece of soft wood, I used a pine door shim and press up on the underside if the molding and simply lift it off the clip from the top.  Start from the back of the door and work forward. Hope this helps.  It saved all of my clips.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||07-06-2001||03:17 PM||||thats the same way to take off moldings on chrys minivans. of course it also depends on how old/brittle the plastic is. I never tried that way on a Fiero though, dont do that many. I have a narrow putty knife with a curled up edge that usually works on most cars fine.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||07-06-2001||07:39 PM||||Well.... on the door skin center trim, you can try pushing the trim down then prying out on the bottom. This is if the clips have any flex in them... you said you replaced some of yours so this should work. On the peice of door trim I have handy the clips only fit one way... This is the old trim. I'm pretty sure the round is the same.<P>If the tab breaks out of the eye that reaches into the door, drop a small wedge in there and tack it with silicone. Or try some rubber/plastic tubing. Have to do this from inside the door....<P>Aero mouding on the doors is held by a combination of clips and rivits. Worse there are a couple diferant systems used. The 2 OE skins I have left over from my window install are put together diferantly and I'm pretty sure they came out of the factory that way.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 07-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||07-07-2001||01:12 AM||||Thanks for the replies.  Actually, I don't think I'll take all the moldings off.  When I repaint the molding, I'll just mask and stuff.  The only one I want to take off is the one for the passenger door; one clip isn't right and is pushing the trim away.  Yes, the clips are less than a year old, and I can tell that they're still a little flexible.  I'll try the methods mentioned and get back to you guys.  Thanks again!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
